          "id": "T3W9K",
          "name": "Atrax robustus",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "Sydney funnel-web spider",
          "lineage": "Sydney Funnel-webs",
          "continents": [
            "Australia"
          ],
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "The Sydney funnel-web spider (Atrax robustus) is a species of venomous mygalomorph spider native to eastern Australia, usually found within a radius of Sydney. It is a member of a group of spiders known as Australian funnel-web spiders. Its bite is capable of causing serious illness or death in humans if left untreated.\nThe Sydney funnel-web has a body length ranging. Both sexes are glossy and darkly coloured, ranging from blue-black, to black, to shades of brown or dark-plum coloured.",
          "sourcedFrom": "wikipedia",
          "wikipediaTitle": "Sydney funnel-web spider",
          "children": [],
          "sourceIds": {
            "gbif": [
              "2145055"
            ],
