          "continents": [
            "Australia"
          ],
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "A funnel-web of Victoria and southern NSW, distinguished by the notably dense scopulae (hair tufts) on the tarsi that give the species its name. Like most Hadronyche it is a ground-dweller in moist forest and heathland, constructing a silk-lined burrow with radiating trip-lines. Medically significant but rarer in urban settings than Atrax robustus.",
