          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "Karawatha funnel-web",
          "lineage": "Tree Funnel-webs",
          "continents": [
            "Australia"
          ],
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "A funnel-web described from Karawatha Forest in the southern suburbs of Brisbane, Queensland — one of the few remaining patches of coastal heath and open eucalypt forest in the greater Brisbane metropolitan region. Its presence in this heavily urbanised landscape makes it an important species for public health awareness. Like other southeast Queensland Hadronyche it constructs a burrow in clay soils with a silk collar.",
          "sourcedFrom": "generated",
          "children": [],
