          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "One of the earlier-described Hadronyche from southeastern Australia, named for the brassy, ochre-tinged colouration of its carapace and legs — orichalcea means 'brass-coloured' in Latin. Found in moist sclerophyll forest in NSW and Victoria. A medium-sized ground-dwelling funnel-web that builds burrows under logs, rocks and in soil banks in shaded gullies.",
          "sourcedFrom": "generated",
