          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "A large funnel-web of tropical and subtropical Queensland, named for its robust build — among the largest Hadronyche species after the closely related H. formidabilis. Found in rainforest and wet sclerophyll forest of northeastern Queensland, where it builds substantial silk-lined burrows. Like H. formidabilis it inhabits tree hollows and root cavities in wetter forest types as well as the ground layer.",
