          "lineage": "Tree Funnel-webs",
          "continents": [
            "Australia"
          ],
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "A funnel-web distinguished by lighter spotting or mottling on the abdomen, in contrast to the typically uniform dark colouration of most Hadronyche. Found in moist forest of eastern Australia. Like all members of the genus, females tend to remain in or near the burrow while males wander extensively during the autumn mating season, which accounts for most human encounters with the family.",
